-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a9a39405-02de-43e3-9265-cf8f153c31a2
-- title:
--   Lemma 1 (Zinkevich) — projected online gradient ascent with $\eta=D/(G\sqrt T)$ has regret at most $GD\sqrt T$
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal K\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ be convex, let $P$ be a Euclidean projection operator onto $\mathcal K$, let $T\ge 1$, and let $D,G>0$ with $\|y-z\|_2\le D$ for all $y,z\in\mathcal K$. Let $f_1,\dots,f_T:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ be reward functions, each concave on $\mathcal K$. Let $x_1\in\mathcal K$ and let $x_2,\dots,x_T$ be generated by the online gradient step (4)
--
--   $$
--   x_{t+1}=P\bigl(x_t+\eta\,\nabla f_t(x_t)\bigr),\qquad \eta=\frac{D}{G\sqrt T},
--   $$
--
--   where each $f_t$ is differentiable at $x_t$ with $\|\nabla f_t(x_t)\|_2\le G$. Then for every $x^*\in\mathcal K$,
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{t=1}^T f_t(x^*)-\sum_{t=1}^T f_t(x_t)\le G D\sqrt T .
--   $$
--
--   The reward functions are arbitrary: $f_t$ may depend on $x_1,\dots,x_t$. This is the regret guarantee that the dual player of Algorithm 1 runs on, once per constraint.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The page bounds $\max_{x^*\in\mathcal K}$; the statement holds for every comparator $x^*\in\mathcal K$, which is the same bound without assuming the maximum is attained. The page's "$G\ge\max_t\|f_t(x_t)\|$" is read as the gradient bound $\|\nabla f_t(x_t)\|$, as the rest of its sentence says. The gradient $\nabla f_t(x_t)$ is the vector $g_t$ of `HasGradientAt`. Convexity of $\mathcal K$ and concavity of the rewards are the OCO setting of p. 4.
-- source:
--   Ben-Tal, Hazan, Koren, Mannor, Oracle-Based Robust Optimization via Online Learning, arXiv:1402.6361v1, p. 5, Lemma 1 (with (4))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SpectralProjGrad_Shared_IsProjOnto

namespace OracleRO.DualSubgrad

/-- Lemma 1 (Zinkevich 2003), p. 5: projected online gradient ascent (4),
`x_{t+1} = P(x_t + η ∇f_t(x_t))` with `η = D/(G√T)`, has regret at most `G D √T` against every
fixed point of `K`, for concave rewards `f_t` on the convex set `K` whose gradients at the iterates
have norm at most `G`, when `D` bounds the diameter of `K`. -/
theorem lemma_1 {n : ℕ} (K : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)))
    (P : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (f : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (g : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (T : ℕ) (D G : ℝ)
    (hK : Convex ℝ K) (hP : SpectralProjGrad.Shared.IsProjOnto K P)
    (hT : 1 ≤ T) (hD : 0 < D) (hG : 0 < G)
    (hdiam : ∀ y ∈ K, ∀ z ∈ K, ‖y - z‖ ≤ D)
    (hconc : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, ConcaveOn ℝ K (f t))
    (hgrad : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, HasGradientAt (f t) (g t) (x t))
    (hgradG : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, ‖g t‖ ≤ G)
    (hx1 : x 1 ∈ K)
    (hstep : ∀ t ∈ Finset.Ico 1 T, x (t + 1) = P (x t + (D / (G * Real.sqrt T)) • g t)) :
    ∀ xs ∈ K, ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t xs - ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, f t (x t)
      ≤ G * D * Real.sqrt T := by sorry

end OracleRO.DualSubgrad
